Viennese jelly roll with fresh fruit
6
Viennese sponge roll filled with vanilla mousseline cream and fresh strawberries.

---
Viennese sponge
whole eggs|225|g
egg whites|135|g
egg yolks|90|g
powdered sugar|250|g
wheat flour|115|g

Vanilla mousseline cream
semi-skimmed milk|500|ml
powdered sugar|120|g
eggs|100|g
pastry cream mix|50|g
soft butter|250|g
vanilla pod|0.5|pcs

Fruit filling
strawberries|250|g

---
Make the sponge: sift the flour.
Beat the whole eggs and yolks with half the sugar to ribbon stage.
Beat the whites to stiff peaks, adding the remaining sugar gradually.
Fold the two mixtures together, then fold in the sifted flour.
Spread the batter onto a baking-paper-lined tray.
Bake at 170°C until evenly golden.
Cool on a rack.

Make the pastry cream: bring the milk to the boil with the split and scraped half vanilla pod, infuse 15 min.
Whisk the eggs with the sugar, add the pastry cream mix (or flour/cornstarch).
Pour the boiling milk over the mixture, mix and return to the pan.
Cook at a boil 3 to 5 min stirring constantly.
Off the heat, add half the cold butter in pieces.
Pour the cream into a bowl, cover with cling film and cool 1 to 2 hours.

Beat the remaining butter until soft.
Whisk the cooled pastry cream to loosen it, then beat in the soft butter to make mousseline.

Wash and dry the strawberries, slice them.
Spread an even layer of mousseline over the sponge.
Arrange the strawberry slices on the cream.
Roll the sponge gently into a tight log.

---
Vary the fruit with the season (berries, pears, peaches…).
Optionally lightly soak the sponge with flavoured syrup (vanilla, lemon, alcohol) before filling.
Let the pastry cream cool fully before adding the butter for a stable mousseline.

---
dessert
roll
biscuit
strawberry
mousseline
